   "titulo": "Use of the future",
   "texto": [
    "The simple futur speaks of something that will happen later or of a prediction: **Un jour, je vivrai à l'étranger** (one day I will live abroad).",
    "To anticipate time or something likely: **Demain, il fera beau** (tomorrow will make good time)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "If + present, future",
   "texto": [
    "In one condition, use **si** + present and then the future: **S'il fait beau, nous irons à la plage** (if it's a good time, we'll go to the beach). In an indirect question, **si** means «si/acaso» and can be followed by the future: **Je ne sais pas s'il viendra** (I don't know if it will come)."
   ]
